  "summary": "Democratic Nordic design uniting light woods, functional simplicity, craft quality and egalitarian beauty.",
  "description": "From Kaare Klint's human-measured furniture to Alvar Aalto's bent birch and the 1954-57 \"Scandinavian Design\" US exhibitions, the Nordic countries built a design identity around affordability, craft and light-chasing interiors: pale wood, wool, ceramics, white walls, daylight. The concept of hygge and lagom informs its cozy restraint. Its everyday ubiquity — IKEA being the mass echo — makes it the most exported European interior language.",
